  <!-- ======================= FAQ ======================= -->
  <section class="sec sec-warm" style="display: none;">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="sec-head centred">
        <p class="eyebrow centred">Common questions</p>
        <h2>Before you call.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq">
        <details open>
          <summary>Do I need an appointment, or can I walk in?</summary>
          <p>
            An appointment is strongly recommended — procedure days fill up and
            walk-ins may face a long wait. The quickest way to get a slot is
            WhatsApp at +91 90922 32991; you will usually be confirmed the same
            day.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What does a consultation cost?</summary>
          <p>
            Consultation is charged separately from treatment and is discussed
            openly when you book. If you proceed with a procedure on the same
            day, the consultation fee is adjusted against it.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Will Dr. Kavitha do the procedure herself?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes — every time. Lasers, injectables, minor surgery and hair
            procedures are performed by Dr. Kavitha personally. Support staff
            assist with preparation and aftercare, not with the procedure
            itself.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Are these treatments safe for darker Indian skin?</summary>
          <p>
            They are — provided the device settings are right. Deeper skin types
            are more prone to post-inflammatory pigmentation, which is why
            device parameters, peel strengths and session intervals at Skin
            Trust are calibrated specifically for Tamil Nadu skin rather than
            copied from a manufacturer's default.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How many sessions will I need?</summary>
          <p>
            It depends entirely on the concern. Hair PRP is typically a course
            over several months; acne scars usually need multiple combined
            sessions; laser hair removal takes six to eight sittings; a mole
            removal is often one visit. The expected number is always given to
            you in writing at the consultation.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you offer EMI or instalment payments?</summary>
          <p>
            Multi-session courses can be paid in instalments. We do not push
            prepaid packages for treatments you may not need — the plan is
            reviewed at intervals and adjusted based on your response.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do you offer laser hair removal for full body?</summary>
          <p>
            Yes. We use a medical-grade Diode Laser which is safe for all Indian
            skin types. Treatment areas include face, upper lip, underarms,
            arms, legs, bikini line and full body. Each session is performed by
            Dr. Kavitha.
          </p>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Where exactly is Skin Trust Hospital?</summary>
          <p>
            No. 28, Chairman Ramanujan Street, Karur — 639001, opposite
            Kamaatchi Amman Temple, Tamil Nadu. Parking is available directly
            outside on the street.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

